    {
      "filename": "Pirca del Inca at Cerro del Plomo.jpeg",
      "title": "File:Pirca del Inca at Cerro del Plomo.jpeg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bc/Pirca_del_Inca_at_Cerro_del_Plomo.jpeg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pirca_del_Inca_at_Cerro_del_Plomo.jpeg",
      "width": 4224,
      "height": 2376,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0",
      "artist": "Tijs Michels",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Pirca del Inca at Cerro del Plomo",
      "description": "Pirca del Inca (approx. 5,100m) at the Cerro del Plomo (5,424m), looking south-south-east.\nFebruary 1954 the Plomo mummy was found at this site.\nIn the background, from left to right: Marmolejo (6,108m), San José (5,856m), Loma Larga (5,404m), Mesón Alto (5,257m).\n\nThe Cerro del Plomo (5,424m) is not to be confused with the Nevado El Plomo (6,070m), which lies on the border about 20km to the north-east. (Cf. John Biggar, The Andes — A Guide for Climbers, ISBN 0-9536087-2-7, p. 217; Hermann Kiendler, Die Anden — Vom Chimborazo zum Marmolejo — Alle 6000er auf einen Blick, ISBN 978-3-936740-36-3, pp. 349–352.)",
      "dateCreated": "2010-03-08",
